meta {
  name: List Order Notes
  type: http
  seq: 13
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/notes
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  ~category: SAMPLE
  ~sampleId: {{sampleId}}
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  List an order's notes for the Order Overview page's Order / Sample / Tech tabs
  (and the Order Console's notes hover cards), newest-first (`createdAt`
  descending). Each row:
  `{ id, category, body, createdByName, createdAt, source, readonly, action?, testName?, sampleLabel? }`.

  - `category` — `ORDER` | `SAMPLE` | `TECH`.
  - `source` — `ORDER` for notes added on the Order Overview page,
    `LAB_REPORT` for the read-only Technician Reporting notes (Order / Sample /
    Tech Notes saved with `POST /lab-reports/:id/notes` on any report of this
    order, any branch; soft-deleted ones, e.g. Tech notes cleared by a Repeat,
    are left out), `ACCESSION` for the read-only accession sample notes merged
    into the SAMPLE stream.
  - `readonly` — `true` for `LAB_REPORT` and `ACCESSION` rows (add/see them on
    the Technician / accession screens, not here). Accession rows also carry an
    `action` (e.g. `collect`).
  - `testName` — `LAB_REPORT` rows only: the test the note was written on (a
    panel member's own test name).
  - `sampleLabel` — `LAB_REPORT` and `ACCESSION` rows: the sample(s) the note
    belongs to, as `"<sample name> · <barcode>"` (comma-separated when a test
    has several samples); `null` when unknown.
  - `createdByName` — the author's resolved name, falling back to the raw
    `Person.id` when the person can't be resolved (`null` only for accession
    rows with no recorded actor).

  Query params:
  - `category` (optional) — one of `ORDER` | `SAMPLE` | `TECH`. Omit to return
    all three tabs together. Every stream merges the Technician Reporting notes
    of the same category; when omitted, or when `category=SAMPLE`, the SAMPLE
    stream additionally merges the order's accession sample notes (from Collect
    Sample / status-update actions) so the complete sample history is shown.
    `GET /orders?includeNoteCounts=true` counts exactly these rows per category.
  - `sampleId` (optional, the sample's id, max 64 chars) — narrow the list to ONE sample of the order
    (the In-House Orders list's per-sample notes icons): the Technician
    Reporting notes of the reports that use that sample (a panel member's
    report only uses its own member test's samples), that sample's own
    accession notes, and every `ORDER`-source note - Order Overview notes are
    saved against the whole order (no sample), so they belong to every sample
    of it (the FE tags them "Whole order"). A sample that is not a live sample
    of this order gets `[]`.
    `GET /accession/order-samples/grouped?includeNoteCounts=true` counts
    exactly these rows per sample (`SAMPLE` / `TECH`).

  404 `ORDER_NOT_FOUND` if the order is missing, soft-deleted, or owned by
  another tenant.
}
